  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, numerically stable reference implementation following exact specifications.\n\n### 💻 Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef nadam_step(w: list, m: list, v: list, grad: list, lr: float = 0.002, beta1: float = 0.9, beta2: float = 0.999, eps: float = 1e-8) -> dict:\n    w_arr = np.array(w, dtype=float)\n    m_arr = np.array(m, dtype=float)\n    v_arr = np.array(v, dtype=float)\n    g_arr = np.array(grad, dtype=float)\n    m_new = beta1 * m_arr + (1.0 - beta1) * g_arr\n    v_new = beta2 * v_arr + (1.0 - beta2) * (g_arr ** 2)\n    m_hat = beta1 * m_new + (1.0 - beta1) * g_arr\n    w_new = w_arr - lr * m_hat / (np.sqrt(v_new) + eps)\n    return {'new_w': np.round(w_new, 6).tolist(), 'new_m': np.round(m_new, 6).tolist(), 'new_v': np.round(v_new, 6).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for memory buffers.\n",
